  "review": {
    "label": "curated_editorial",
    "look_ahead": "The 2025-26 season would bring European league-phase football, a cup defence and a relegation worry, ending with Thelin's dismissal and Stephen Robinson's appointment.\n",
    "read": "This is the record's central case. A fan can point to the Scottish Cup as proof that the project works, or to five wins in 27 as proof that it does not. Both are true descriptions of the same season. The value of the record is to keep them together and ask which parts are structural and which are variance.\n",
    "trade_off": "The cup win and the league collapse are not separate stories. A squad good enough to win a final can still be too thin, too young or too inconsistent to hold a league season. The trading model's upside and its variance appear in the same season.\n",
    "what_did_not": "The league run after the start was poor: only five wins in 27 games. The League Cup semi-final was a 6-0 defeat. The season did not produce a stable style or a settled league position.\n",
    "what_worked": "The Scottish Cup was won, the club sold Miovski for a club-record fee and the new manager produced a start that briefly looked like a step change. The cup final performance showed the squad could compete with the best team in the country.\n"
  },
